118:## Execution shell
119:
120:Every command in this plan is POSIX shell and MUST be run under Git Bash.
121:Verified present on this host: `/usr/bin/bash` (Windows path
122:`C:\Program Files\Git\usr\bin\bash.exe`), GNU bash 5.3.15(1)-release,
123:x86_64-pc-cygwin. Also verified on PATH: `env`, `grep`, `sort`, `comm`,
124:`sha256sum`, `mktemp`, `wc`, `git`, `docker`, and `go` (go1.24.13
125:windows/amd64). Verified **absent**: `jq` â€” no command in this phase may depend
126:on it. PowerShell is this workspace's interactive default and will fail on
127:`env -u`, on `test -z`, and on `$(...)` capture semantics; do not run these
128:commands there.
129:
130:**Pipeline rule.** A bare `go test â€¦ 2>&1 | grep -c X` reports grep's exit
131:status, not the test process's, so a build failure, a panic, an unexpected
132:success and a zero-test run all satisfy it. Every check in this plan therefore
133:either runs under `set -o pipefail` or uses the capture form: assign the combined
134:output to a variable, capture `$?` on the next statement, and assert status and
135:content as separate conditions.
136:
137:**Skip-counting rule.** `go test -json` emits `"Action":"skip"` for packages with
138:no test files as well as for skipped tests. Measured at the phase base over
139:`./...`: 49 skip events, of which **38 carry a `"Test"` field** and 11 are
140:package-level. Every skip count in this phase must filter for `"Test":"`, or use
141:`-v` and count lines matching `^--- SKIP`, which was independently measured at 38.
