210:## Verified ground truth
211:
212:Measured in this repository at commit `030521b` before planning, by running the
213:commands. Do not re-derive; do not assume anything beyond these.
214:
215:- **Phase base commit: `030521b1ec7c12df868445bf8d162527202d42f1`.** Verified at
216:  planning time: `git rev-parse --verify` succeeds,
217:  `git merge-base --is-ancestor 030521b HEAD` exits 0,
218:  `git log --format=%H 030521b..HEAD -- Makefile .github/workflows/ci.yml` prints
219:  nothing, and `git diff --name-only 030521b..HEAD` filtered against `^internal/`
220:  and `^\.planning/` prints nothing. The cycle-1 base `fcebad1` failed both of the
221:  last two checks, because `868d45b` landed after it and modified
222:  `.github/workflows/ci.yml`. Ancestry alone is not a sufficient guard, which is
223:  why Task 1 carries a `<precondition>` asserting all four properties.
224:- `go test ./... -count=1` at the phase base exits 0 with **38 test-level skips**
225:  and no database present. `-shuffle=on` yields the same 38. Call sites per file:
226:  `authorreturn_test.go` 9, `runrejection_test.go` 7, `researchunit_test.go` 6,
227:  `segmentation_decision_test.go` 6, `segmentation_test.go` 5, `papers_test.go` 5
228:  â€” 38 total, re-measured at `030521b`.
229:- `pgxpool.New` is lazy. With `postgres://u:pw@127.0.0.1:1/nodb?sslmode=disable`
230:  it returns a nil error; the failure surfaces at `Ping`.
231:- The `Ping` error names the host and omits the password, and is constructed by
232:  pgx from the parsed config rather than from the raw DSN. Observed on both DSN
233:  forms: ``failed to connect to `user=u database=nodb`: 127.0.0.1:1 (127.0.0.1):
234:  dial error: â€¦``. It does disclose the user and database name.
235:- **Correction to cycle 1 â€” pgx v5.7.2 redacts the password in its parse error.**
236:  Cycle 1 recorded that the parse error "echoes the connection string verbatimâ€¦
237:  so a malformed DSN carrying a password would publish it". That is false for the
238:  pinned version. Measured on four shapes, all with a distinctive token in the
239:  password position, all against the **unmodified** helper: URL form renders
240:  `u:xxxxxx`; keyword/value form renders `password=xxxxx`; a `?password=` query
241:  parameter renders `password=xxxxx`; a `?sslpassword=` query parameter renders
242:  `sslpassword=xxxxx`. The token count in the output was `0` every time. Any
243:  acceptance criterion asserting "the password does not appear" therefore passes
244:  with zero code written and proves nothing.
245:- **What pgx does echo verbatim is everything else in the DSN.** Measured with a
246:  distinctive token in the *database-name* position: the parse error printed
247:  ``cannot parse `postgres://u:xxxxxx@ bad host/<token>``` and
248:  ``cannot parse `host=x port=notanumber password=xxxxx dbname=<token>``` â€” token
249:  count `1` in both cases, at the phase base, unmodified. That is the falsifiable
250:  control this plan uses: a criterion that **fails today** and can only pass once
251:  the branch stops interpolating the DSN and the pgx error. See T-01-01.
252:- The existing helper classifies a parse error as fatal (`t.Fatalf`) and an
253:  unreachable host as a skip (`t.Skipf`). With the flag unset and a closed-port
254:  DSN, `TestSaveRun_FixtureRoundTripsAllOffsets` reports `--- SKIP` and the
255:  package exits 0 â€” verified. That branch must survive unchanged.
256:- A non-test Go package that imports `testing` builds, vets and formats clean, and
257:  `t.Skip` called from it correctly skips the calling test. Verified with a probe
258:  module on Go 1.24.
259:- `go.mod` requires `golang-migrate/v4`, `google/uuid`, `pgx/v5 v5.7.2`,
260:  `godotenv`, `goldmark`. **There is no testify dependency**, contrary to
261:  PROJECT.md's Constraints line. Use stdlib `testing` only; adding a dependency is
262:  out of scope for this plan.
263:- Local DSN for the compose service:
264:  `postgres://epistemicos:epistemicos@localhost:5432/epistemicos?sslmode=disable`
