92:## Execution shell
93:
94:Every command in this plan is POSIX shell and MUST be run under Git Bash â€”
95:verified present on this host at `/usr/bin/bash` (`C:\Program Files\Git\usr\bin\bash.exe`),
96:GNU bash 5.3.15(1)-release, x86_64-pc-cygwin. `jq` is verified **absent**; no
97:command may depend on it. PowerShell is this workspace's interactive default and
98:will fail on `test -z` and on the capture forms used below.
99:
100:**Pipeline rule.** A bare `go test â€¦ 2>&1 | grep -c X` reports grep's exit status,
101:not the test process's, so a build failure, a panic or a zero-test run all satisfy
102:it. Every check here either runs under `set -o pipefail` or captures the combined
103:output and `$?` separately and asserts them as independent conditions.
