91:Every command in this plan is POSIX shell and MUST be run under Git Bash.
92:Verified present on this host: `/usr/bin/bash` (Windows path
93:`C:\Program Files\Git\usr\bin\bash.exe`), GNU bash 5.3.15(1)-release,
94:x86_64-pc-cygwin. Also verified on PATH and used below: `env`, `grep`, `sort`,
95:`comm`, `sha256sum`, `cut`, `mktemp`, `wc`, `git`, `docker`, and `go` (go1.24.13
96:windows/amd64). Verified **absent**: `jq` â€” no command in this plan may depend on
97:it, which is why the `-json` checks below use `grep` rather than a JSON parser.
98:PowerShell is this workspace's interactive default; `env -u`, `test -z`, `trap`
99:and `$(â€¦)` capture will not behave there. Launch Git Bash explicitly.
100:
101:**Pipeline rule.** A bare `go test â€¦ 2>&1 | grep -c X` reports grep's exit status,
102:not the test process's. A build failure, a panic, an unexpected success and a
103:zero-test run all satisfy such a check. Every scenario below therefore uses the
104:capture form: assign the combined output to a variable, capture `$?` on the *next*
105:statement, and assert status and content as separate conditions. Where a pipeline
106:is genuinely more readable, `set -o pipefail` must be in effect first.
107:
108:**Skip-counting rule.** `go test -json` emits `"Action":"skip"` for packages with
109:no test files as well as for skipped tests. Measured at the phase base over
110:`./...`: 49 skip events, of which **38 carry a `"Test"` field** and 11 are
111:package-level. Every `-json` skip count in this plan filters for `"Test":"`. The
112:`-v` method â€” counting lines matching `^--- SKIP` â€” was independently measured at
113:38 and the two must agree.
114:
115:## Artifacts this phase produces
116:
117:This plan produces **no code symbols**. Its only artifact is its SUMMARY, which is
118:listed in `files_modified`.
119:
120:The new symbols this phase creates belong to plans 01-01 and 01-02 â€” the
121:`internal/platform/testenv` package with its exported `URLEnv`, `RequireEnv`,
122:`Required`, `Pool` and `Fixture` and its unexported `hostFromURL` and
123:`unparseableURLMsg`; the `EPISTEMIC_OS_TEST_REQUIRE_DB` environment variable; and
124:in the segment domain the unexported `preambleInvariant` and the new
125:`TestPreambleInvariant_Control`. See those plans' artifacts tables.
126:
127:`EPISTEMIC_OS_DB_URL`, `make gate`, `make up`, `make migrate`,
128:`TestSaveRun_FixtureRoundTripsAllOffsets`, `TestFixtureIntegrity` and the CI
129:workflow are all pre-existing and are read, never written, by this plan.
130:
131:## Flagged assumptions â€” spec-less edge probe
132:
133:No SPEC exists for this phase. The deterministic edge probe over GATE-04 and
134:GATE-05 returned 4 applicable edges. After cycle 1, three have been given the
135:referent they actually have in this phase and authored as explicit criteria in
136:`01-01-PLAN.md`'s `must_haves.truths`. One remains unresolved and is reproduced
137:here because this is the plan a human reviews, and it may not be silently dropped.
138:
139:| # | Requirement | Category | Probe | Status | Where |
140:|---|---|---|---|---|---|
141:| E1 | GATE-04 | unclassified | (no category was assigned, so there is no probe question to answer) | **unresolved â€” flagged** | queued for disposition in Task 3 |
142:| E2 | GATE-05 | adjacency | When two things are exactly equal or just touch, do they merge, collide, or separate? | **resolved â€” explicit** | `01-01` truth: `Pool` decides in a documented order and names exactly one cause; `Fixture` runs only after `Pool` returns |
143:| E3 | GATE-05 | empty | What is the result for empty, single-element, or null input? | **resolved â€” explicit** | `01-01` truth: empty flag value is false; empty and keyword/value DSNs yield an empty host and a fixed placeholder |
144:| E4 | GATE-05 | ordering | When elements compare equal, is output order specified and stable? | **resolved â€” explicit** | `01-01` truth: outcome is independent of execution order; `-shuffle=on` yields the same 38 |
145:
146:Accounting: **4 surfaced == 3 authored into `must_haves.truths` + 1 flagged.**
147:E1 is not dismissed by the planner; the executor must not dismiss it either.
